{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Felix George <felix.george@ibm.com>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": [], "description": "OpenTelemetry MCP Instrumentation\n\n<a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp/\">\n    <img src=\"https://badge.fury.io/py/opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp.svg\">\n</a>\n\nThis library allows tracing of agentic workflows implemented with MCP framework [mcp python sdk](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk).\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp\n```\n\n## Example usage\n\n```python\nfrom opentelemetry.instrumentation.mcp import McpInstrumentor\n\nMcpInstrumentor().instrument()\n```\n\n## Privacy\n\n**By default, this instrumentation logs prompts, completions, and embeddings to span attributes**. This gives you a clear visibility into how your LLM application tool usage is working, and can make it easy to debug and evaluate the tool usage.\n\nHowever, you may want to disable this logging for privacy reasons, as they may contain highly sensitive data from your users. You may also simply want to reduce the size of your traces.\n\nTo disable logging, set the `TRACELOOP_TRACE_CONTENT` environment variable to `false`.\n\n```bash\nTRACELOOP_TRACE_CONTENT=false\n```\n\n## Diagnostics\n\nA failure inside this instrumentation never reaches your application: the traced call still goes out, and its result -- or its own exception -- is what the caller sees. Such a failure is logged at `WARNING` on the `opentelemetry.instrumentation.mcp` logger, with the stack at `DEBUG`.\n\nSome of these failures sit on a per-message path (the stream writer), so a persistent one logs a line per MCP message. To quiet it without touching the rest of your logging:\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nlogging.getLogger(\"opentelemetry.instrumentation.mcp\").setLevel(logging.ERROR)\n```\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": null, "home_page": null, "keywords": null, "license": null, "license_expression": "Apache-2.0", "license_files": null, "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "name": "opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp/", "project_urls": {"Repository": "https://github.com/traceloop/openllmetry/tree/main/packages/opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp"}, "provides_extra": ["instruments"], "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/opentelemetry-instrumentation-mcp/0.63.1/", "requires_dist": ["opentelemetry-api<2,>=1.38.0", "opentelemetry-instrumentation>=0.59b0", "opentelemetry-semantic-conventions-ai<0.6.0,>=0.5.1", "opentelemetry-semantic-conventions>=0.63b1", "mcp; extra == \"instruments\""], "requires_python": "<4,>=3.10", "summary": "OpenTelemetry mcp instrumentation", "version": "0.63.1", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "release_dates": {"0.39.4": "2025-04-30T08:09:00.985147Z", "0.40.10": "2025-06-17T11:07:38.722046Z", "0.40.11": "2025-06-17T19:00:38.481638Z", "0.40.12": "2025-06-20T19:15:59.303041Z", "0.40.13": "2025-06-24T06:12:01.071979Z", "0.40.14": "2025-06-24T10:25:56.731115Z", "0.40.2": "2025-04-30T10:01:03.838887Z", "0.40.3": "2025-05-07T11:49:38.343829Z", "0.40.4": "2025-05-10T10:08:36.178272Z", "0.40.5": "2025-05-13T19:28:42.464210Z", "0.40.6": "2025-05-16T14:39:05.298904Z", "0.40.7": "2025-05-20T15:04:28.642491Z", "0.40.8": "2025-06-09T00:22:28.713913Z", "0.40.9": "2025-06-10T09:54:15.066364Z", "0.41.0": "2025-07-13T20:06:11.093134Z", "0.42.0": "2025-07-17T19:45:30.875482Z", "0.43.0": "2025-07-22T08:30:31.390365Z", "0.43.1": "2025-07-23T14:39:10.078657Z", "0.44.0": "2025-08-03T21:05:58.456284Z", "0.44.1": "2025-08-04T08:39:35.826514Z", "0.44.2": "2025-08-11T19:51:53.871612Z", "0.44.3": "2025-08-12T10:34:54.666933Z", "0.45.0": "20